---
Why Apache-2.0 and not "all rights reserved":

This project's entire thesis is that a stranger can check the claims. Default
copyright makes that legally impossible -- a reviewer may read the code but not
run, fork, or redistribute the verifier. A verification thesis shipped without
a licence is a verification thesis nobody is permitted to act on.

IBM's qcode-discovery catalogue rows reproduced in the release bundle remain
under their own upstream licence; nothing here relicenses them.
